  "content_body": "Suzanne Chan, D.N.P., C.L.C., C.P.S.T.\n\nAbout Suzanne Chan, D.N.P., C.L.C., C.P.S.T.\n\nSuzanne Chan is a board-certified pediatric nurse practitioner working in the Infant Cardiac NICU at NewYork-Presbyterian Morgan Stanley Children's Hospital in New York City. In addition to her expertise in labor and delivery, Chan is also a certified lactation counselor (CLC) and a Certified Passenger Safety Technician (CPST).\n\nChan has not only earned a Bachelor of Science and Master of Science in Nursing, but also a Doctorate of Nursing Practice from Columbia University in New York City.\n\nBoard certification\n\nChan is board certified by the Pediatric Nursing Certification Board.\n\nHospital affiliation\n\nChan is affiliated with NewYork-Presbyterian Morgan Stanley Children's Hospital in New York City.\n\nOther relevant positions\n\nChan is a member of the American Nurses Association (ANA), the National Association of Pediatric Nurse Practitioners (NAPNAP), the American Association of Nurse Practitioners (AANP), and the American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP).\n\nShe lives in New York with her husband, three children, and their beloved dog.\n\nThe educational health content on What To Expect is reviewed by our medical review board and team of experts to be up-to-date and in line with the latest evidence-based medical information and accepted health guidelines, including the medically reviewed What to Expect books by Heidi Murkoff. This educational content is not medical or diagnostic advice. Use of this site is subject to our terms of use and privacy policy. © 2005-2026 Everyday Health, Inc., a Ziff Davis company.\n\nOpens a new window",
